<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Drones called home in time, and their wrecks taken home (D'thorga Patches 0.39.0, D'thorga Framework 0.240.0;
    docs/development/drone-recall-design.md; the owner's report of 23 Nov 2026). Fortified Features Framework's drones (The Dead Man's
    Switch's uca, erima, trashpan, hound, wildfowl and the rest) carry Fortified.CompDrone and the game's mechanoid power cell, and are
    sent home by their own comp only when two hours of power are left, whatever the distance. In the owner's save they mostly died of a
    flat cell on the way, giving their platform nothing back and leaving 58 wrecks. This names the comp, so D'thorga Framework calls a
    drone home once its power barely covers its walk home, and haulers carry wrecks home, where the platform takes back their steel.

    The names are members of Fortified.CompDrone as read on 23 Nov 2026 (the build of that day): PlatformOwner (the platform, or the pawn
    wearing or carrying it), ReturnToPlatform(bool forceInterrupt) and Props.returnToDraftPlatformJob. 180 ticks is the wait in
    Fortified's JobDriver_ReturnToPlatform before a drone is taken in. Fortified's own call at two hours still stands. Loaded only with
    Fortified Features Framework. An addition, not a fix of a fault; docs/development/temporary-patches.md notes it under "Left out on
    purpose". Not yet tested in game.
  -->
  <Phobos.Framework.Recall.PhobosRecallDef>
    <defName>PhobosRecall_FortifiedDrone</defName>
    <label>drone</label>
    <compClass>Fortified.CompDrone</compClass>
    <homeMember>PlatformOwner</homeMember>
    <recallMethod>ReturnToPlatform</recallMethod>
    <returningJobMember>Props.returnToDraftPlatformJob</returningJobMember>
    <dockTicks>180</dockTicks>
  </Phobos.Framework.Recall.PhobosRecallDef>
</Defs>
